<p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/052R">Definition <span data-tag="052R">3.5.4.1</span>.</a> Let $n$ be an integer. We say that a simplicial set $X$ is <em>weakly $n$-coskeletal</em> if the restriction map </p>
<div class="equation">
  \[  \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}}( \Delta ^{m}, X ) \rightarrow \operatorname{Hom}_{\operatorname{Set_{\Delta }}}( \operatorname{\partial \Delta }^{m}, X) \]
</div>
<p> is a bijection for $m \geq n+2$ and and injection for $m = n+1$ (provided that $n \geq -1$). </p>
</article>
